WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.700
Fester's Quest.

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:07.600
It's just a kidnapping of an entire city by an alien UFO.

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:10.800
Will Fester sit still for this?

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:33.820
Nostalgia! And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.460
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:45.040
And I'm Joe. You know, going by the back of the box, they seem to be aware of the lunacy that is Fester's Quest.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:53.020
I mean, I was expecting lunacy from Adam's family, but this is just not the kind of lunacy that I expected.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.840
It's just that the back of the box to me just doesn't...

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:58.840
I don't get it.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.740
Does Uncle Fester sit still a lot?

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:03.440
Or like, what is the sit still thing?

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.100
Am I missing something really obvious?

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.360
I actually don't know too much about Adam's family.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:16.500
Like, I mean, I imagine I watched some of it as a kid, but I don't know any of the deep lore.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:22.040
Me neither. I'd love to find out that he's a character that's like, you know, usually in a wheelchair.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.480
And then in this game, he finally gets up out of the wheelchair and walks everywhere.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:26.960
But I don't think that's true.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.160
I don't know what the sit still line is for.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:33.800
But the rest of it kind of makes sense because that, you know, it's just a kidnapping, right?

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.940
Of an entire city by aliens.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:41.680
Like, all right, cool. Like, I think they're aware of what they've set out to do.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:50.180
And, you know, if nothing else, the experience of the start of this game where the story is communicated to you, you don't have to read the back of the box of the manual.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:54.880
They actually have, before you ever press start, cut scenes that show all this to you.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:01.340
So that, for me, was enough of a selling point that I was like, all right, I'm ready for weird.

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:20.100
Yeah. And again, I just, I think it's a missed opportunity to make it, like, alien invasion weird because the whole series is sort of based off of this macabre, like, just sort of Victorian horror thing.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.340
But sure, I'm ready for weird.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:28.340
Yeah. And, you know, we thought Scrooge, Scrooge McDuck was weird last week.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:43.500
You know, now getting a whole game where you can only ever play as one particular member of the Addams Family and choosing it to be Uncle Fester as just the very first Addams Family video game ever made just feels like a bizarre decision.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:54.440
I could understand if they're, like, planning a Addams Family video game universe where you'll be able to play, like, each one has their own game and this is just the first in the line with Fester's Quest.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.320
But this is pretty much it as far as where Addams Family games go.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:09.320
That factoid actually surprises me because usually there's some obscure Atari 2600 game that's happened before these.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.220
So, wow.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:14.120
I'm amazed we're actually finally seeing the first of something.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:22.180
Yeah. My question for you guys, which it sounds like you guys also are not, like, big Addams Family fans.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:23.700
So maybe you won't know the answer either.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:31.740
But, like, is Uncle Fester, like, normally, like, some badass, like, gunslinging, like, character?

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.020
Like, it's just...

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:41.360
I don't know. From not knowing anything about the Addams Family, my guess is this does not represent Uncle Fester in the way most people see him in the show.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:42.800
I could be totally wrong there.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.220
Is his gun usually depicted as, like, a megaphone?

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.580
Yeah. Yeah, I think it's...

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.180
It's like a weird horn-looking thing.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.940
It's not really, like, a revolver.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:56.020
I mean, it's like a cartoon blasted-back rifle thing.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:57.340
It's like an alien gun.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:58.680
Oh, okay.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.820
I wasn't thinking alien gun.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:04.000
I was just thinking, like, maybe a 1700s gun.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:06.860
Something. Yeah, like one of those, like...

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:07.900
I was thinking, like, a bugle.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:09.980
He's just got a trumpet.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:14.040
Well, you could start at a lot of different places when you want to talk about this game.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:22.540
I did want to just mention that on top of the whole, like, cinematic experience of the cutscene at the top of when the game starts,

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:29.740
there is something really strange about the sudden juxtaposition right after that with the Fester's Quest title screen

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:35.400
looking like something that one of the children of the developers at Sunsoft had just decided to make.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:37.820
It's all crazy colors.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:42.100
It's not really, like, a, you know, a design.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:42.940
It's not themed.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:48.160
Yeah, it's not themed for a pinata or something, like a party, you know?

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.880
Here we have the Addams Family music.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:54.840
Yeah, we have the Addams Family music playing, though,

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:59.940
and I guess that lets you know that at least they got the intellectual property rights to make this game.

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:02.040
No, they just bought Fester.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:07.080
But, see, I'm going to just get this theory out of the way right now.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:11.880
Were we pretty certain this was created as some other game and then they just slapped Addams Family skin on it?

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.500
Oh, I mean, that's...

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.900
That was my thought the whole time. It almost seems more than likely, but...

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:23.200
Yeah. Because it seems like it was going for this, like, very, like, badass kind of...

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:31.180
Even, like, the music in the regular game just does not sound like it's trying to, you know, invoke Addams Family.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:32.980
No, you're probably right.

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:37.100
Right. I kind of agree with this baseless assessment.

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:41.660
Yeah, well, good. That's most of my assessments are baseless anyways, so I'm glad I could get something out of it.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:45.520
And I don't know if, Mike, if you know this, but they did something similar with Doki Doki Panic,

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:47.700
because that's what Super Mario Bros.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:54.020
2 is. I've heard that urban legend once or twice in my life, but thank you for confirming that they did do that.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:55.880
No problem. I'd like to just keep you up on that.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:58.920
Yeah. Now, here's the thing about Fester's Quest, though.

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:02.480
I don't see anything that says that this is a Doki Doki Panic situation.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:09.980
And keep in mind, Sunsoft made, you know, Blaster Master, which is a, you know, a game that...

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:15.540
It sounds like it's weird that I'm bringing that up, but, like, a lot of the portions of Fester's Quest,

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:21.800
like, certainly not the 3D aspects, but, like, this top-down thing is very similar to Blaster Master's format

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:28.040
of when you get out of the, you know, the vehicle and then start going in the top-down levels.

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:30.900
I feel like this is similar to that in some regards.

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:35.420
So they basically just had an engine and probably acquired a license and said,

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:39.440
eh, well, we already know what we can do, so let's just make that, but with the Addams Family.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:40.480
Now, how do we do that?

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.060
Yeah, that would make sense, too.

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:47.140
So Fester's Quest is a run-and-gun adventure game.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:51.940
Adventure being kind of nice to the whole idea of, you know, the quest that you go on here.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:56.820
But basically, as I mentioned, the entire city has been abducted by aliens,

00:06:56.820 --> 00:07:00.800
and now only Uncle Fester can traverse through the neighborhood,

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:07.900
try to track down basically the monsters that have somehow found their way onto the land

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:12.660
to reveal pieces to the puzzle that will get him to the alien's UFO ship,

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:16.420
and he'll be able to take them down and free the entire city.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:19.000
That sounds pretty epic in scale.

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:24.660
I'm sure we all know after playing this game for a little bit that you're mostly being reduced to

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:29.880
exploring the neighborhood, exploring the sewers, and exploring the buildings,

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.540
which is, like, the 3D aspect of this.

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:35.280
Rather than talk about what you do in this game,

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:37.680
I want to start with Fester himself here.

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:41.080
You know, this is the character you're going to be playing as throughout the entirety of the game.

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:45.800
He's this balding old man, not something I feel like kids would feel.

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:48.100
You know, it's, like, cool to be Donatello or Leonardo.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.520
It's not cool to be Uncle Fester.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:54.220
So what does it feel like to control Uncle Fester here?

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:55.760
Feeble Fester, if you will.

00:07:56.140 --> 00:08:00.160
I mean, he controls relatively normally,

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:05.240
for the most part, if he hasn't been licked by an enemy,

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:11.800
in which case he feels like a personification of frustration.

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:15.580
But in general, if you have not been licked,

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:17.480
if Fester has not been licked,

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:20.280
he feels normal enough.

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:22.860
He's slow, but, like, it's tight.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:24.480
Yeah, I agree.

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:26.820
As far as, like, literally the controls of, like,

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:28.820
how he moves and the inputs,

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.260
it's perfectly fine.

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:32.340
It doesn't mean that there aren't other problems

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:33.240
with the way the game,

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:38.080
the way that your inputs interact with the environment and stuff,

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.680
but as far as actual walking,

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.140
it feels great. Yeah, when you shoot,

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:44.600
when you press the shoot button,

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:45.940
he shoots. Yeah.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:48.160
In a straight line at first.

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:49.940
Yeah. Which is important.

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:52.280
Which is intuitive. Yeah, it's intuitive.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.780
So I called him Feeblefester

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:57.480
because I don't know how you guys felt,

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:59.400
but the version of him

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.180
that we start the game off with, right,

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:02.200
the base character,

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:03.640
if this was an RPG,

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.580
he would be, like, level negative seven.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.120
He's so powerless at the beginning of this game

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:11.840
compared to the enemies around him.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:13.400
The very first enemy in the game,

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:15.320
the Goomba of this game, if you will,

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:19.160
is something that takes, like, seven hits to kill.

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:21.820
And for me, I'm just wondering,

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:25.500
why even start the game on that kind of scale?

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:26.880
You know, it doesn't bode well

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.840
when a game's primary strategy

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:29.980
at the very beginning

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:32.680
is grinding enemies senselessly

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:34.640
to collect all the power-ups

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:35.740
that you possibly can

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:37.300
to be strong enough

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:39.580
to then make it through the rest of the game.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:41.540
When the start of the game is grinding,

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:45.420
it's like, imagine if Dragon Warrior started

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:47.240
and the slimes that you fight

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:48.160
right outside the city

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:50.820
are incredibly tough encounters

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:52.200
where it's like, every single time,

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.300
it's like, oh, you just made that out

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:54.840
by the skin of your teeth. You gotta go back to the city

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:56.900
and heal now and then go back out there

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:59.200
and fight another one for just two experience points.

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:00.660
That's kind of what it felt like

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.300
for me at the beginning of Fester's Quest here.

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:03.780
Well, it doesn't just stop there.

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:05.860
It's like, and we've had games

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:07.660
that start off like really rough

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:09.520
but then after a while

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:11.280
you start to get used to it

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:13.260
or the problem starts to subside

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:15.080
because you've grown into,

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:18.760
you've grown into some power yourself.

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:21.760
But no, this entire game

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:25.020
has enemies that will always

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:25.900
just take forever

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:27.380
for one reason or another.

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:28.680
Yeah, and it gave me,

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:29.920
especially that happening

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:30.720
with that first enemy,

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:31.920
I don't know if the Goomba

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:33.160
of this game that you're talking about, Mike,

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.100
is that weird, like,

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:36.060
that weird, like, spiky ball thing

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:37.460
that just literally doesn't move.

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:40.540
But that, first of all,

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.500
should not be anything.

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:43.340
It's not an enemy.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:44.920
It doesn't attack you. You just have to shoot it

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:45.760
to get power-ups

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:46.800
a bunch of times.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:47.940
But then second of all,

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:49.380
you run into shortly thereafter

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:50.720
one tiny enemy

00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:52.020
that moves a little bit.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:53.840
And because it moves

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:56.180
and you take 40 hits to kill it,

00:10:57.280 --> 00:10:58.760
it gives me the immediate

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.100
first impression of, like,

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:01.720
the first impression of this game

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:03.900
is the grind that usually

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:05.480
comes much later in a game,

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:06.700
like, this tediousness.

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:08.740
Like, it starts off,

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:10.020
in my opinion, on the wrong foot.

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:10.960
Yeah, I feel like

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:12.380
just make Fester stronger

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:14.140
or the enemies weaker, right?

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:15.240
You don't have to make Fester

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:16.400
this ultimate powerful thing

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:17.380
if you want to build up,

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:18.600
you know, the idea that

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:19.900
over time your gun

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:22.100
will get stronger and you'll acquire this whip.

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:23.180
And don't worry about

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:24.640
the light bulbs. Like, they'll be things

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:26.160
that you find rather than just

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:28.120
hopefully they randomly spawn

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:30.080
from the enemies that you kill.

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:32.220
Instead, they could have

00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:33.140
just made the enemies

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:34.260
just weaker altogether

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:35.480
at the start of this game.

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:36.860
You know, I'm not saying

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:38.260
that they should have been one-hit kills,

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:39.580
but it is absurd

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:41.160
how much it takes, especially when

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:42.440
you have to start this game

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:43.460
grinding for

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:45.300
hoping that you get keys

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:46.700
or hoping that you get light bulbs

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:47.700
so that you can progress

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:49.000
throughout this game.

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:50.360
I was even just watching

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:52.520
a Let's Play of this game,

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:53.960
and funny enough,

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:55.460
Let's Plays, for those of you that don't know,

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:57.960
I feel like they are framed perfect

00:11:57.960 --> 00:11:58.900
a lot of the times.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:01.400
Like, there are somebody who's just putting the inputs in

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:02.520
and getting the game to go through.

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:03.580
It's not somebody's, like,

00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:06.060
actual playthrough of those games.

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:08.080
You never really see anybody die

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:10.280
in a long play.

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:11.320
I mean, it depends, but yeah, I know what you mean.

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:13.500
Most of the time, it's a perfect run.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:14.720
Right, in those

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:16.480
World of Long Plays videos,

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:18.640
you know, obviously, like, if it's a person

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:19.440
with a personality,

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:20.840
you know, they'll,

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:22.600
you know what I mean? You know, it's like

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:23.920
the World of Long Plays ones

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:25.280
are just the actual

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:26.480
raw gameplay footage,

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:28.320
and it feels like they're programmed

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:29.640
to do exactly what you'd have to do

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:30.600
to show the full game

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.700
from beginning to end. This one had, like,

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:34.440
an extra little slice of comedy

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:38.280
at the start where the Fester goes out there

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:39.760
and immediately dies.

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:40.880
Like, they make a point

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:41.980
to show you that, like,

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:43.300
this game can end

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:45.240
very quickly if you're not paying attention,

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:46.480
and then they show you

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:48.320
the full run without Fester ever

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:49.540
taking another hit

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:50.560
in the game, and I thought

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:52.080
that was a very cheeky

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:53.400
of World of Long Plays

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:54.280
to go and do that.

00:12:54.760 --> 00:12:55.580
Start the game

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:58.300
with the game over. And yeah,

00:12:58.420 --> 00:12:59.600
that was sort of my experience.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:02.040
I died pretty quickly,

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:04.160
and then, because I usually,

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:07.100
because I do have the ability to do turbo,

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:09.340
